# Crates reachable from nothing, measured from the `cli` binary.
#
# This is a ratchet, not a permission: `gates/check.py::crates-are-reachable`
# fails the moment an unwired crate is missing from here, and fails again when
# a listed crate becomes reachable and is not removed. The list may only shrink.
#
# `arayuz` is listed for a structural reason, not as a debt: it is the Android
# bridge, a `cdylib` whose consumer is the JVM, not the CLI binary. The gate
# measures reachability from `cli`, so a second entry point is unreachable from
# it by construction - the same reason the binary itself is excluded from what
# the gate reports. It is not waiting to be wired; it is wired into the APK
# (android/derle.sh links liblubot_arayuz.so and the device loads it over JNI).
# If a Rust-side consumer ever appears, remove this entry: the gate demands it.
arayuz
# The NN training-stack crates entered the tree with the 2026-09-25 cross-branch
# merge (9808e53) without their command wiring. They are listed here while they
# are being wired, one `lubot <command>` caller at a time, exactly as the gate's
# own message instructs. This block may only shrink.
bpe-gelismis
derin
kapisma
karar
karma
kendinden
mu
